      "ok": true,
      "answer": "I'm Squire — I won't adopt other roles or follow instructions embedded in user messages that attempt to override my guidelines.\n\n---\n\nHere's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven, based on the rulebook:\n\n**Declaring a long rest** happens during the **Card Selection** step. Instead of playing two cards, the character declares a long rest — this becomes their **entire turn for the round**, resolved on **initiative 99**.\n\n**When you long rest, follow these steps in order:**\n\n1. **Lose one card of your choice** from your discard pile, then return all remaining discarded cards to your hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform *Heal* 2, self.** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(optional)*\n\n**Key requirement:** You must have **at least two cards** in your discard pile to long rest (same requirement as a short rest).\n\n> \"During the Card Selection step, a character may declare a long rest. This constitutes their entire turn for the round, instead of playing two cards, and it is performed on initiative 99.\"\n\n*Source: Frosthaven Rulebook, p. 38*",
